-- ============================================================================
-- tests-independent-open.l4 -- four assertions of the independent test author (see tests-independent.l4) that
-- ASSERT A READING THE ENCODING DOES NOT TAKE and that the lead triaged as genuinely open on the text
-- ("assumed, not ruled", NOTES.md fork register).  Each is EXPECTED TO FAIL on both builds; check.sh lists
-- the module in expected_failed with the count 4, and NOTES.md records them as findings.
-- Do not edit an expected value to make them pass: the other reading is the encoding's.
-- ============================================================================

-- Q57 Art 4(7)
#ASSERT `Under Article 4(7), as a controller, am I a controller of this processing` `legal person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Q125 Art 6(3)
#ASSERT `Under Article 6(3), as a controller, is the basis for my processing laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which I am subject` `Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Q178 Art 8(1)
#ASSERT `Under Article 8(1), as a controller, may a Member State provide by law for this lower age` 12 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Q232 Art 9(2)(h)
#ASSERT `Under Article 9(2)(h), as a controller, does point (h) (health or social care) apply to my processing` `Art 9(2)(h) some other purpose` TRUE `Art 9(2)(h) Union law` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
